[0.023, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;193;7m⚠\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;255;193;7mCode Mode (experimental) is on · this session can be resumed only with Code Mode on\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mI want to provide a set of standards for the artists to author the assets against. The engine supports Principled \u001b[39m    \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mBRDF Metal workflow and will have meshlets clusters, cluster forward rendering, raycasting shadows and reflections. \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mSuggest a good set of standards, naming conventions, file layouts to keep it all on track. Leave the budgets up to \u001b[39m   \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mthe artists for now. Help me draft a\u001b[40Gset\u001b[44Gof standards for \u001b[63Ge artist\u001b[72G to use. I don't think UV\u001b[98G are cove\u001b[108Ged yet but \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bwe will need six for some asset typ\u001b[40G, and\u001b[46Gperhaps more, so i\u001b[65G the\u001b[70Ge\u001b[72Gis a way to have a flexible number o\u001b[109G UVs for a \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bshad\u001b[8Gr then we\u001b[18Gn\u001b[20Ged to discuss it \u001b[38Gnd ensure the documentation reflects tha\u001b[80Gmeth\u001b[85Gd\u001b[87Gif it is select\u001b[103Gd.\u001b[39m             \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B                                                                                                                    \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mYou should examine industry b\u001b[33Gst practices, but tail\u001b[57G them\u001b[63Gfor this\u001b[72Gparticular engine because this is a greenfield \u001b[39m \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mproj\u001b[8Gct and\u001b[15Gshouldn'\u001b[24G be weighed down\u001b[41Gby th\u001b[48Gdeca\u001b[53Ges of \u001b[60Gech debt tha\u001b[73G o\u001b[77Ger\u001b[80Gengines have\u001b[94Gncurr\u001b[100Gd.\u001b[39m   \r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B\u0