[0.036, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[3G-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mDecision ledger:\u001b[22m a new\u001b[28G\"Art st\u001b[36Gndards\"\u001b[44Ggroup with D-118 (Manif\u001b[68Gst defi\u001b[76Ges\u001b[79Gthe\u001b[83Gstandards)\u001b[94Gand D-119 (the art\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Breposito\u001b[14Gy on Git LFS).\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BBoth lanes have\u001b[19Ga note so\u001b[29Gthe\u001b[33Gother\u001b[39Gsession\u001b[47Gsees\u001b[52Gthey're\u001b[60Gtaken.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2BRenaming the \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mmetallicRoughness\u001b[39m slot\u001b[39Gto \u001b[38;2;177;185;249morm\u001b[39m in J66 is my addition,\u001b[69Gnot\u001b[73Gsomething\u001b[83Gyou\u001b[87Gasked\u001b[93Gfor.\u001b[98GI\u001b[100Gadded\u001b[106Git\u001b[109Gso\u001b[112Gthe\u001b[116Gslot\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bmatches\u001b[11Gthe\u001b[15Gmap\u001b[19Gword,\u001b[25Gbut\u001b[29Git\u001b[32Gmeans\u001b[38Grewriting\u001b[48Gevery\u001b[54Gexisting\u001b[63Gmaterial\u001b[72Gfile\u001b[77Gin\u001b[80Gboth\u001b[85Grepos\u001b[91Gwhen\u001b[96Git\u001b[99Glands.\u001b[106GShould\u001b[113GI\u001b[115Gcommit\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bboth branc\u001b[15Gs?\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m✻\u001b[3GBrewed for 2m 52s · done 12:19 pm\r\u001b[2B※\u001b[3G\u001b[1mrecap: \u001b[22m\u001b[3mI'm writing the art standards, defined in Manifest and supported by Jettison. The Manifest doc and Jettison's \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Broadmap items J64 to J67 are drafted, uncommitted, in lanes B and C. Next, you decide whether to commit both branches \r\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m\u001b[3mand whether to keep the `orm` slot rename. (tur\u001b[52Goff r\u001b[58Gcaps in /config)\u001b[23m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mmake that rename, then commit both branches\u001b[39m                                                      