[0.016, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[3G \u001b[5Grepository on Git LFS).\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BBoth\u001b[8Glanes\u001b[14Ghave\u001b[19Ga\u001b[21Gnote\u001b[26Gso\u001b[29Gthe\u001b[33Gother\u001b[39Gsession\u001b[47Gsees\u001b[52Gthey're\u001b[60Gtaken.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BRenaming\u001b[12Gthe\u001b[16G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mmetallicRoughness\u001b[34G\u001b[39mslot\u001b[39Gto\u001b[42G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249morm\u001b[46G\u001b[39min\u001b[49GJ66\u001b[53Gis\u001b[56Gmy\u001b[59Gaddition,\u001b[69Gnot\u001b[73Gsomething\u001b[83Gyou\u001b[87Gasked\u001b[93Gfor.\u001b[98GI\u001b[100Gadded\u001b[106Git\u001b[109Gso\u001b[112Gthe\u001b[116Gslot\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bmatches the map word, but it means rewriting every existing material file in both repos when it l\u001b[101Gn\u001b[103Gs.\u001b[106GShould I commit\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bbo\u001b[6Gh branches?\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m✻\u001b[3GBrewed for 2m 52s · done 12:19 pm\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m※\u001b[3G\u001b[1mrecap: \u001b[22m\u001b[3mI'm writing the art standards, defined in Manifest and supported by Jettison. The Manifest doc and Jettison's \r\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m\u001b[3mroadmap items J64 to J67 are drafted\u001b[41Guncommitted, in lanes B\u001b[65Gand C. Next,\u001b[78Gyou decide whether to commit both branches \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Band whether to keep the `o\u001b[30Gm` slo\u001b[37G rename. (turn off recap\u001b[63Gin /config)\u001b[23m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mmake that rename, then commit both branches\u001b[39m                                                                           \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mSearching\u001b[13Gfor\u001b[17G\u001b[1m1\u001b[19G\